  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved compliance and safer working environments</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ministry of Legal Affairs, Labour &amp; Consumer Affairs (MLLCA) of Grenada aims to strengthen labour management relations by improving dispute settlement processes and implementing a stronger inspectorate function. The ILO will provide technical support to enhance the conciliation mechanism for labour disputes resolution, with financial and technical backing from the ILO. This initiative will promote social dialogue and harmonious labour relations.

Additionally, the ILO will support the development of a strategic compliance plan for labour inspection to ensure the successful implementation and enforcement of labour legislation. The MLLCA also seeks ILO assistance in reviewing the Occupational Safety &amp; Health Policy to include the right to a safe and healthy work environment in the Labour Code amendments.</narrative>
  </description>
